Replace MediaProjection with Accessibility Service for screen capture

The MediaProjection approach showed a system "Cast your screen" dialog on every
capture — a full-screen consent prompt designed for screen recording, not for
screenshots. On Android 14+ it asked "Single app or entire screen?" with
wording about "casting", which confused users into thinking the app was about to
stream their display.

The Accessibility Service uses takeScreenshot() (API 30+), which grabs one
frame silently. The trade-off is a one-time toggle in Accessibility Settings
instead of a per-capture system dialog. Once enabled, every subsequent tile tap
is instant with no interruption.

Bonus: AccessibilityEvent.TYPE_WINDOW_STATE_CHANGED tells us which app the user
was looking at when they tapped the tile. That becomes the Memory's
sourcePackage — genuinely useful context that MediaProjection could not provide
without a separate UsageStatsManager query.

What this service does NOT do:
- Read keystrokes, screen text, or node trees. canRetrieveWindowContent is false
  in the XML config, so the system does not deliver accessibility nodes.
- Monitor the screen continuously. The capture happens once, on explicit command,
  then nothing until the next command.
- Run without the user having granted it. The Accessibility toggle is a system
  setting the user enables knowingly and can revoke at any time.

Removed:
- ScreenCaptureService (the foreground service)
- ScreenCapturePermissionActivity (the MediaProjection consent broker)
- ScreenFrameConverter (row-stride arithmetic for ImageReader frames — not
  needed since takeScreenshot() delivers a HardwareBuffer)
- FOREGROUND_SERVICE and FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PROJECTION permissions
- The CHANNEL_CAPTURE_SERVICE notification channel (was for the FGS notification)

The QS tile now checks whether the accessibility service is enabled. If not, it
opens Android's Accessibility Settings and posts a notification explaining what
to do. If enabled, it sends a command to the running service.

592 unit tests, 0 failures. assembleDebug, assembleRelease and lintDebug clean.
